<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 42 — Failure Modes & Cascading Failures.
    resilience/  Backoff (exponential, full jitter), RetryBudget, RetryPolicy, Deadline (propagated as an absolute
                 time), QueueAgeShedder (refuse work that waited too long or whose caller has given up), P2cBalancer
    web/         order-service: a deadline filter, deadline propagation and budgeted retries as RestClient
                 interceptors, Spring Framework 7's @ConcurrencyLimit and @Retryable with non-default settings
  verify/run.sh runs five experiments against real HTTP services on loopback: queueing near saturation, retry
  amplification through three tiers, a metastable failure, a reconnect herd, and tail latency at fan-out.
-->
